  /* ── MOVED OUT OF SPEC_NAME_I18N (2026-08-12) ───────────────────────────
     63 option translations had been written into SPEC_NAME_I18N, which the
     product form reads ONLY for schema names: SchemaSpecsSection resolves
     options with useTranslation(SPEC_I18N), so every one of these fell back
     to English for zh/ar readers — the whole ironing/finishing option
     vocabulary, silently, since it shipped.
     57 moved here (their keys did not already exist in SPEC_I18N). SIX were
     left behind because the two dictionaries disagree about what the key
     means: o:rotary (Rotary | Rotary Drum), o:single (Single Phase | Single
     Head), plus o:jeans / o:shirts / o:dresses / o:trousers which are true
     duplicates. Merging those needs a decision on which meaning wins — a
     wrong merge relabels a live field, so they stay put and stay reported. */
